  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on a single fiscal year (2022) across Spanish municipalities with more than 50,000 residents, which may limit generalizability to smaller towns or different national governance systems.",
      "what": "This study analyzed the relationship between gender balance in local governments and municipal service delivery performance using data envelopment analysis and regression models. The sample comprised 102 Spanish municipalities with populations over 50,000 during the 2022 fiscal year. The analysis revealed that greater gender balance within the municipal government team improves service delivery performance specifically when a female mayor is in office, with further performance gains observed under the interaction of right-wing female mayors and gender diversity.",
      "why": "It demonstrates that the performance benefits of gender diversity in local cabinets are contingent on leadership characteristics, showing that gender balance does not automatically improve efficiency unless paired with a female mayor."
    }
  },
